tructure reveals the unique origin of an interspecific chromosomal inversion (2La) in the <italic>Anopheles gambiae</italic> complex.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>103</volume><fpage>6258</fpage><lpage>6262</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16606844</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001249-Besansky1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Besansky</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Caccone</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamm</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Molecular phylogeny of the <italic>Anopheles gambiae</italic> complex suggests genetic introgression between principal malaria vectors.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>91</volume><fpage>6885</fpage><lpage>6888</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8041714</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001249-dellaTorre1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>della Torre</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Merzagora</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Coluzzi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Selective introgression of paracentric inversions between two sibling species of the <italic>Anopheles gambiae</italic> complex.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>146</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9136013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001249-Slotman1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surna